  "summary": "ACLU NorCal case page describing Lagleva v. Doyle, a 2021 lawsuit alleging Marin County Sheriff Robert Doyle illegally shared ALPR data with ICE, CBP, and out-of-state agencies in violation of California's SB 34 and SB 54. A May 2022 settlement bound the Sheriff and successors to stop sharing ALPR data with agencies outside California.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "community activists sued Marin County Sheriff Robert Doyle for his practice of illegally sharing millions of local drivers' license plate numbers and location data with hundreds of federal and out-of-state agencies, including Immigration and Customs Enforcement and Customs and Border Patrol.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Sheriff Doyle has agreed to stop sharing license plate and location information with agencies outside of California to comply with state laws S.B. 34 and S.B. 54.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
